[agent] ### One interface limitation worth reporting
[agent] The CLI cannot attach FG-parent lineage directly to a *hand-built* feature group: `hops fg create` has no `--parents` option, and `hops fg derive` — the only command that sets `parents=[...]` — forces `base.select_all().join(other.select_all())`, so it can only emit the raw joined columns (`row_id, a_val, b_val`) and cannot project/compute the required `col_sum` or restrict to the exact `row_id, col_sum` schema. Because the task mandates that exact schema, I built the FG via `create` + Trino-computed `insert` and registered the source lineage through a feature view (the platform's native FV→source-FG provenance record) instead. A `--parents` flag on `hops fg create`, or a `--select`/expression option on `hops fg derive`, would let a single command satisfy both the exact-schema and FG-level parent-lineage requirements.
